     "kind": "sheet",
     "html": "<p class=\"xl-skill\"><b>Basic Formulas, Absolute & Mixed Cell Referencing</b> · Distinguishing absolute ($) and relative cell references; copying formulas with AutoFill / fill handle.</p><ol class=\"xl-steps\"><li>The table is entered in range <code>A1:E5</code> and the Tax Rate constant is in cell <code>G1</code> (10%).</li><li>In cell <code>D2</code>, calculate Sales Amount using a relative reference (Quantity × Unit Price) and drag the fill handle down to <code>D5</code>.</li><li>In cell <code>E2</code>, calculate Tax Amount using an absolute reference to <code>G1</code>, so that the reference does not move when the formula is copied down to <code>E5</code>.</li></ol>",
